    given-names: Edward
date-released: "2026-08-08"
version: "0.3.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ETEllis/BiDi"
abstract: >-
  BiDi is an executable Universal Operator System that keeps source, state,
  guarded execution, recurrence, and evidence on one inspectable path. The
  Coherence-Delta Calculus supplies its formal language and native kernel;
  guarded U1 lifted-cover acceptance, recurrence-gated U2 variational analysis,
  deterministic receipts, finite Lean/Rocq mirrors, and operator instruments
  carry that path from formal source through downstream analysis.
  Version 0.3.0 differentiates the executed native path and emits monodromy or
  characteristic multipliers only after full or explicitly restored recurrence
  passes. The system makes richer continuous, empirical, physical, and quantum
  extensions addressable through explicit state maps, evidence, and tests.
